
====================================================================================================
S1. Saturation ceilings -- the numbers the frozen text does not state
====================================================================================================
  As N -> infinity, sigma_tot -> sigma_sym, so every separation has a CEILING in sigma that
  no sample size can beat. These are the decision-relevant figures.
  pair               |delta gamma|    ceil@0.01   ceil@0.02   ceil@0.05   ceil@0.10
  Newton vs MI               0.090         9.00        4.50        1.80        0.90
  MI vs MG                   0.047         4.70        2.35        0.94        0.47
  Newton vs MG               0.137        13.70        6.85        2.74        1.37
  MI vs MOND                 0.240        24.00       12.00        4.80        2.40
  [OK] at the frozen sigma_sym = 0.02, Newton-vs-MI ceilings at 4.50 sigma (decidable) while MI-vs-MG ceilings at 2.35 sigma (not) -- consistent with the prereg's own pre-declaration
  [OK] if the symmetric systematic were 0.10, even Newton-vs-MI would ceiling at 0.90 sigma -- so the credibility of sigma_sym is not a detail, it decides whether Front A is a test at all

====================================================================================================
S2. The statistical-only sample-size caveat, quantified
====================================================================================================
  Newton-vs-MI at 3 sigma, statistical only:      N >=   12033   (frozen text: 12200)
  Newton-vs-MI at 3 sigma, sigma_sym included:    N >=   21660   (factor 1.80)
  [OK] the frozen 12200 is reproduced to 1% by a statistical-only calculation, confirming what its own label says

====================================================================================================
S3. *** THE ONE-SIDED BUDGET -- why a blanket widening is the WRONG fix ***
====================================================================================================
  The prereg records: 'contamination only pushes gamma UP'. A one-sided error folded in
  quadrature would (a) inflate the error on the NEWTON side, where the systematic cannot
  reach, making a Newton verdict artificially weak, and (b) under-state it on the MI/MG side,
  where it can, making an MI verdict artificially strong. Both are wrong, in opposite
  directions. The correct treatment: gamma_true <= gamma_hat, so
      Newton-side test (is gamma_hat consistent with 1.00 from ABOVE?):  use sigma_sym only
      MI/MG-side test (is gamma_hat really as high as it looks?):        subtract delta_up
   delta_up  gamma_hat needed for a 3-sigma MI claim               lands in
       0.00                                    1.083     MI-compatible band
       0.05                                    1.133     MI-compatible band
       0.10                                    1.183           MG-side band
  [OK] at delta_up = 0.10 an MI claim would require gamma_hat >= 1.183, which the prereg's own frozen bands assign to the MG-SIDE (1.145-1.20), not to the MI-compatible window. So an MI claim would need a measured value the bands read as MG -- a self-veto rather than a mis-claim. (My first assertion said this reached the >1.20 contamination-guard zone; it does not, it stops in the MG band. Corrected.)
  AND THE ASYMMETRY IS A GIFT, not a cost: a Newton-side verdict is UNAFFECTED by delta_up,
  so the most likely decisive outcome in DR4 is a KILL of the MI branch, not a confirmation.
  Newton-side: gamma_hat <= 1.055 would put MI at >2 sigma
  disfavoured regardless of how bad the contamination is.

====================================================================================================
S4. The declared fork on delta_up, with a pre-stated survival requirement
====================================================================================================
  delta_up cannot be known before the DR4 NSS screen is exercised, so it is declared as a
  FORK -- the same discipline the corpus uses for the a0 footing -- not fitted afterwards:
      delta_up = 0.00   the frozen-as-is reading (NSS screen assumed fully effective)
      delta_up = 0.05   NSS screen credited with cutting the DR3-era disagreement ~5x
      delta_up = 0.10   pessimistic; NSS screen credited with ~2.5x
  VERIFIED LITERATURE INPUT (fetched, not remembered; force gamma -> gamma_v = sqrt):
      Banik+24 (MNRAS 527, 4573)       gamma_force = 1.000  ->  gamma_v = 1.000
      Chae 2023                        gamma_force = 1.430  ->  gamma_v = 1.196
      Chae 2024a                       gamma_force = 1.490  ->  gamma_v = 1.221
      Hernandez+2024b                  gamma_force = 1.500  ->  gamma_v = 1.225
      Chae 2026 (arXiv:2601.21728)     gamma_force = 1.600  ->  gamma_v = 1.265
      gamma_v spread = 0.265
  AND THE DISAGREEMENT IS NOT SOFT -- it is MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE HIGH-SIGNIFICANCE CLAIMS:
      Banik+24 reports 19 SIGMA preference for Newtonian (gamma_force = 1)
      Chae 2023 reports gamma_force = 1.43 +/- 0.06, which is 7 sigma FROM 1
  Two groups, overlapping data, incompatible claims at >7 sigma each, differing on exactly
  the systematic the prereg allots 0.02 to. That is a stronger case for Amendment 3 than the
  'spread' framing I first used, and it was only visible after verifying the citation.
  For scale, the unmitigated published disagreement is 0.26, so even the
  pessimistic fork assumes the DR4 screen removes 62% of it.
  SURVIVAL REQUIREMENT (pre-declared): a non-Newtonian verdict counts only if it holds at
  ALL THREE delta_up values. A verdict that appears only at delta_up = 0 is to be reported as
  'contamination-limited', never as support.
  [OK] the pessimistic fork (0.10) still assumes the DR4 NSS screen removes 62% of the published disagreement -- stated so the assumption is visible rather than buried

====================================================================================================
S5. What Amendment 3 must carry
====================================================================================================
  1. The SATURATION CEILINGS of S1, printed next to the sample-size figures, because the
     ceiling (4.50 sigma Newton-vs-MI, 2.35 MI-vs-MG at the frozen
     sigma_sym) is the decision-relevant number and the sample size is not.
  2. The note that 'N >~ 12200' is STATISTICAL-ONLY and becomes N >~ 21660 with
     sigma_sym included. No frozen number is changed by saying so.
  3. The ONE-SIDED split sigma_sym = 0.02 (unchanged) PLUS delta_up >= 0 for residual
     contamination, with the asymmetric scoring rule of S3. This is an ADDITION, not a
     revision: the frozen symmetric machinery is untouched and still runs.
  4. The three-value FORK on delta_up and the survival requirement of S4.
  5. The explicit statement that this amendment makes the framework HARDER to confirm and
     EASIER to kill, which is why it must be filed pre-data. Filed after DR4 it would be
     unusable.
  6. The audit provenance: the amendment exists because the frozen sigma_sym = 0.02 is 13x
     smaller than the 0.26 published disagreement on gamma_v and does not itemise
     undetected companions.
  [OK] the amendment's obligations are enumerated and each is backed by a computed number
====================================================================================================
